



The program allows students to read and respond to other student papers,
and provides the instructor with a way to present a field questions that
are useful for considering outside of class.  For example, Dr. Anne
Woodlief has the program set up to store a series of questions or things
to think about while reading different texts.  The students are able to
"grab" and edit electronic copies of the questions that Dr. Woodlief has
presented and store their reading responses on their private account.
When response papers are assigned, the student has her own reading
responses outlined along with the questions the instructor has asked.


The program allows students to copy files from their accounts to a place
where other students in their class can read and respond to these files.
