What is Grab & Share?

Grab & Share are the two basic functions of the Electronic Writers'
Workshop.  A student is able to write a document using WordPerfect 5.0
on the networked DEC computer system and execute a \fBmacro\fP that runs
a c-shell script.  The shell script provides the student with a menu,
instructing the student to choose an option: grab a file, share a file,
turn in a paper to your professor, or exit.  

GRAPHIC

A student may share her file, allowing her classmembers and professor to
read it, by choosing the share option.  THe student is given a list of
\fBfolders\fP and is asked to choose the folder with which she wishes to
share her file.

The student is then given a list of the files in her account and is
asked to type in the name of the file she wishes to share.  The share
option copies the selected file from the student's account to the folder
allowing other students to read and copy and comment on the student's
text.  


A student may grab a file, allowing her to read and edit a copy of any
file in on of the folders, by choosing the grab option.  Again, the
student is given a list of folders and is asked to choose a folder.
The student is then given a list of available files in the folder they
have chosen and is asked to choose the fielname of the folder they wish
to grab.  After the student enters the filename, the grab option places
a copy of the file they have chosen into their account, where they can
read and edit it.  

The submit option  allows students to turn in papers to their professor.
The student is given a list of her files and is asked to enter the name
of the file she wishes to submit.  A copy of the file is sent to the
instructor's "box"  allowing the instructor to read, print, edit or
perform any WordPerfect function with the students file.  



